## Stage 0 Exit Sign-off

The "Status" column is this dimension's real, current state. The "Gets a
never-blocks exception?" column is a fixed property of the dimension
itself (only Dimension 5's legal carve-out, and the narrow prior-art
sub-check inside Dimension 3, have one) — it does not mean a dimension
with "No" here is already cleared, and it does not mean Dimension 3 as a
whole is exempt (only its prior-art sub-check is). **Read the two
columns together, not the second one alone**: a dimension whose Status
is "in progress" still blocks Phase 1 code regardless of what its
exception column says (a real point of confusion in an earlier version
of this table, found and fixed after an adversarial review pass,
2026-09-22/23).

| Dimension | Status | Gets a never-blocks exception? |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Product | {{cleared / in progress / not started}} | No |
| 2. Project & Scope | | No |
| 3. Architecture & Code | | No overall — but see this dimension's own prior-art sub-check above, which may stay inconclusive without blocking |
| 4. Developer/Practitioner UX | | No |
| 5. Legal/Compliance | | **Yes** — informational only, never blocks |
| 6. UI/UX Vision | | No (even if the answer is "no vision yet, deferred" — that's still a real, recorded answer) |
| 7. Data & Security | | No |

**Human sign-off statement (required, verbatim, not implied):**

> "{{Cleared to start Phase 1 code — date, name.}}"

Once signed off, this file becomes historical record — don't keep editing
it for routine feature work afterward; that's what the regular Definition
of Done and `OPEN-RESEARCH-QUEUE.md` are for. Re-run Stage 0 (a new copy,
not an edit to this one) only for a genuinely new product direction later.
